Let us assume that the body makes vibrations in the new period <math>2\pi p</math>, and let us put <math>x = \text{B} \sin pt</math>; substituting in (22) we have <math>-p^2\text{B} + n^2\text{B} + \text{P}/\text{M} = 0</math>, whence
{{block center|<math>\text{B} = \frac{\text{P}}{\text{M}} \cdot \frac{1}{p^2 - n^2},</math>}}
and the “forced” oscillation due to <math>-\text{P} \sin pt</math> is
{{block center|<math>x = \frac{\text{P}}{\text{M}} \cdot \frac{\sin pt}{p^2 - n^2}.</math> (23)}}
